     Sys(5L)               OS-9 (News)               Sys(5L)     NNAAMMEE                  Sys  - this file describes the mechanism to forward         received articles to other sites or to programs.       DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN                     This files    specifies   the   newsgroups   and         distributions  to  be  forwarded to another site or         to  be  pipe'd  to  a  program.  So you are able to         limit  the  amount  of  articles to be forwarded by         area     (distribution)     or/and    the    topics         (newsgroups).       FFOORRMMAATT                  The format of the file is         <system>{> <flags>}:<newsgroups>:<dists>{:<program>}         where  <<ssyysstteemm>> is in general the system to forward         the  news  (or an ID for programs).  You can append         a  list  of other systemnames (seperated by a slash         //  form  the  main  system), which are seperated by         commas   to  stop  forwarding  articles  which  had         already  passed  these  systems.  The <<ffllaaggss>> are a         list   of  flags  which  are  inserted  before  the         filename   in   the   batchfile.  These  flags  are         interpreted  by  sbatch only. The <<nneewwssggrroouuppss>> is a         list  of newsgroups which are in regular expression         format  (using  Henry  Spencer's regular expression         library),   seperated   by  spaces.   Internal  the         expression  will  be enclosed with ^^ and $$ to allow         only  exact matches.  <<ddiissttss>> are the distributions         which  aren't  regular  expressions,  but  they may         contain  the  meta  characters ?? and ** to match one         (?)   or   zero   or   more   (*)  characters.  The         <newsgroups>   and   <dists>   field  allow  a  not         operation  by  prefixing an expression with an !! so         you  can select specific items not to be forwarded.         If  an  article should be forwarded the filename is         written  in  a  file  in  //hh00//SSPPOOOOLL//BBAATTCCHH  with the         filename  equal  to  <system>  (if  possible). This         file  is  used  by  ssbbaattcchh  to  send  the  articles     Page 1                            Printed (22 Dec 1992)     Sys(5L)               OS-9 (News)               Sys(5L)         themselves.              The <<pprrooggrraamm>>  is  optional  but  if it is given         the  filename  of  the article isn't written to the         file  mentioned  above  but  the  article itself is         pipe'd  to  this  program (so the program must read         the article from stdin).              If the  first  character  of <program> is a plus         sign  then  the rest will be used as a full path to         a  directory  where  to  store  the  articles  with         increasing  numbers.  If  the  first character is a         minus  sign  then  the  rest  is  a  full path to a         directory  which  is  used  instead  of  the  batch         directory (/h0/SPOOL/BATCH).              Each line  in  this file may be continued in the         next  line  if  the  last  character in the prvious         line had been a backslash.              If a  line starts with a colon (::) then the rest         of  the line is taken as a filename of a file to be         included.   With  this  features  it is possible to         create  one  file  for  each  system  which  can be         changed  from  remote  via  mail.  For this purpose         the   program   rreemmssyyss   can   be   found  in  this         distribution.       EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS                      myfeed:!local.* to\.myfeed !to\..* .*:!local *             subfeed:(sub|muc)\..*:sub muc world             save:.*source.*:*:save_it         mmyyffeeeedd  will get everything expect these newsgroups         which  are  prefixed  by llooccaall or have distribution         llooccaall  or  have the prefix ttoo..  and not followed by         myfeed.   ssuubbffeeeedd  will  only  receive  groups of a         local  are (Newsgroups prefixed by muc. or sub. and         distribution  muc  sub  and  world). The entry ssaavvee         will   store   (assuming   a  proper  program)  all         articles in source groups.       Page 2                            Printed (22 Dec 1992)